WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.500
Forge interface captures and recorded simulations.

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.900
Replays run at 1×. Holds and camera views are labeled.
No physical prototype was built or tested.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.900
Recorded simulation at 1×.
Inspection quadruped with 12 actuated joints.

4
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:19.900
The native Forge CAD view shows a feasible concept with checks still open.

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:25.900
Design · native. Select a part: mass, envelope, joints and fasteners.

6
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:31.900
Design · native. The exploded assembly, in the native viewer.

7
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:37.900
Design · native. A section through the assembly.

8
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:44.300
Test · native. Its recorded step test, replayed in the app with contact forces.

9
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:50.700
Test · native. Revisions compared on the same recorded tests.

10
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.900
Wall requirement: at least 0.8 mm.

11
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:57.200
Both earlier screw-pilot walls measure 0.51 mm.
The earlier sampled screen passed both.

12
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:01.700
The revised checker covers declared holes.
Later revisions made those pilots shallower.

13
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:04.400
Checker results on synthetic known-answer cases.

14
00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:13.800
Sensor-pod fixture comparison from recorded states.

15
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:19.700
Ring chamfer 0.4 → 3.0 mm. Key-slot flare 0 → 3.0 mm.
Both changes were tested together.

16
00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:24.200
Recorded fixture comparison at 1×. Same disturbance.

17
00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:27.730
Closer camera, same recorded instant.

18
00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:32.630
Final yaw (limit 3.3°):
Original 3.42° fails. Revised 0.07° passes.

19
00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:39.530
Simulated reference approach: 96/100 original, 100/100 revised.
Chamfer and slot flare changed together.

20
00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:44.130
Faster approach, same 100 held-out pairs.
Original 91/100, revised 98/100.

21
00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:49.630
Draw 630111: original height error 3.977 mm and tilt 10.4° fail.
Revised height error 0.0018 mm passes.

22
00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:56.630
Forge · native study view. The same records in the native study view, with counts.

23
00:01:56.930 --> 00:02:03.630
Forge · native study view. The fast approach profile, side by side in the app.

24
00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:08.330
Same agent, tools and budgets. Feedback differed.
All 54 planned held-out episodes ran.

25
00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:12.730
Passes: A0 14/18, A1 17/18, A2 18/18.
Ten first failures became selected passes.

26
00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:18.630
A2 − A1: +0.056. 95% bootstrap interval [0.000, 0.167].
No established improvement from richer feedback.

27
00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:21.430
Held-out repair results by condition and task family.

28
00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:31.730
Gantry planning with torque, speed and tray-slip limits.

29
00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:36.700
Baseline and optimized trajectories at 1×.
Same path, controller and disturbance.

30
00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:41.230
Contact phase ends. Final recorded state held.

31
00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:49.130
Gantry planned motion: 21.760 → ≈7.474 s.
Simulated transfers: 59/100 → 58/100.
Transfer reliability did not improve.

32
00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:52.030
Baseline and optimized speed along the fixed path.

33
00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:00.030
Planned torque versus the modeled limits.

34
00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:16.130
Modeled mean good units, FIFO / CP-SAT:
Original fixture 11.9 / 13.4. Revised fixture 12.3 / 13.9.

35
00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:19.730
Model and simulation evidence.
No physical robot or fixture validation.

36
00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:24.430
Tier B replays one reference-profile fixture pair.
It requires separately authorized meshes.

37
00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:29.230
Gantry trays remained unseated in 40/100 trials per profile.
Repair feedback superiority was not established.

38
00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:32.630
Design → check → matched test → study → limits.

39
00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.330
Design. Test. Improve.
